  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef Ada constructed a simple undirected graph GGG with NNN vertices (numbered 111 through NNN) as follows:\n\n\nStart with a complete graph with KKK vertices and K⋅(K−1)/2K \\cdot (K-1)/2K⋅(K−1)/2 edges.\nThen, add N−KN-KN−K vertices one by one. After adding each vetex, find some clique of K−1K-1K−1 vertices in the graph and connect the new vertex to all the vertices of that clique.\nConsider NNN boolean variables X1,X2,…,XNX_1, X_2, \\ldots, X_NX1​,X2​,…,XN​ and their negations ¬X1,¬X2,…,¬XN\\neg X_1, \\neg X_2, \\ldots, \\neg X_N¬X1​,¬X2​,…,¬XN​, corresponding to vertices of the graph. You are given the initial values of all variables.\n\nA CNF boolean expression is defined as a conjunction of clauses, where each clause is a disjunction of two or more elements of the set of variables and their negations.\n\nUsing the graph GGG, Ada wrote a CNF boolean expression BBB with MMM clauses, where each clause corresponds to a clique in the graph with some (maybe none) of the variables (corresponding to vertices) negated. More formally, for each iii from 111 to MMM:\n\n\nAda chose some clique in the graph, consisting of LiL_iLi​ vertices Z1,Z2,…,ZLiZ_1, Z_2, \\ldots, Z_{L_i}Z1​,Z2​,…,ZLi​​\nthen for each valid jjj, Ada chose a variable Pi,jP_{i,j}Pi,j​ as either XZjX_{Z_j}XZj​​ or ¬XZj\\neg X_{Z_j}¬XZj​​\nthe iii-th clause in the expression BBB had LiL_iLi​ terms: Pi,1∨Pi,2∨…∨Pi,LiP_{i,1} \\lor P_{i,2} \\lor \\ldots \\lor P_{i,L_i}Pi,1​∨Pi,2​∨…∨Pi,Li​​\nAda wants the expression to evaluate to \"true\". In order to achieve that, she may change the values of variables; for each valid iii, the cost of changing the value of XiX_iXi​ (from \"true\" to \"false\" or vice versa) is CiC_iCi​. Find the minimum total cost needed to make the expression BBB evaluate to \"true\" or determine that it is impossible.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤101 \\le T \\le 101≤T≤10",
      "1≤N,M≤1441 \\le N, M \\le 1441≤N,M≤144",
      "3≤K≤93 \\le K \\le 93≤K≤9",
      "each character of SSS is either '0' or '1'",
      "1≤Ci≤2561 \\le C_i \\le 2561≤Ci​≤256 for each valid iii",
      "1≤Li≤N1 \\le L_i \\le N1≤Li​≤N for each valid iii",
      "1≤∣Pi,j∣≤N1 \\le |P_{i,j}| \\le N1≤∣Pi,j​∣≤N for each valid i,ji,ji,j",
      "Subtasks**Subtask #1 (25 points, time limit 1 second):** K=3K = 3K=3"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains three space-separated integers NNN, MMM and KKK.\nThe second line contains a single binary string SSS with length NNN describing the initial values of the variables. For each valid iii, the iii-th character of SSS is '1' if XiX_iXi​ is true or '0' if XiX_iXi​ is false.\nThe third line contains NNN space-separated integers C1,C2,…,CNC_1, C_2, \\ldots, C_NC1​,C2​,…,CN​.\nMMM lines follow. For each valid iii, the iii-th of these lines contains an integer LiL_iLi​ followed by a space and LiL_iLi​ space-separated integers representing the variables Pi,1,…,Pi,LiP_{i,1}, \\ldots, P_{i,L_i}Pi,1​,…,Pi,Li​​. For each valid iii, the variable XiX_iXi​ is represented by the integer iii and its negation is represented by −i-i−i.",
    "outputFormat": "For each test case, print a single line containing one integer ― the minimum cost needed to make the boolean expression evaluate to \"true\", or −1-1−1 if it is impossible.",
