        "explanation": "Explanation:\nExample case 1: The following figure depicts the graph used to generate the expression.\n\nThe boolean expression is B=(X1∨¬X2∨X4)∧(X2∨X3∨¬X5)∧(X1∨¬X3∨X2)B = (X_1 \\lor \\neg X_2 \\lor X_4) \\land (X_2 \\lor X_3 \\lor \\neg X_5) \\land (X_1 \\lor \\neg X_3 \\lor X_2)B=(X1​∨¬X2​∨X4​)∧(X2​∨X3​∨¬X5​)∧(X1​∨¬X3​∨X2​).\nOne optimal solution is to change the values of X1X_1X1​ and X3X_3X3​."
